pywhat/Data/phone_codes.json
----------------------------
Country calling codes (ITU-T E.164) and their countries. Most of the country names are those
of the GitHub gist "Country and Dial or Phone codes in JSON format" by Goles, or of a fork of
it: https://gist.github.com/Goles/3196253
Added in 2021 (commits 71cdefb and f1c993d).

Licence: not recorded; the gist states none.


pywhat/Data/mastercard_companies.json
-------------------------------------
MasterCard issuer prefixes (BINs) and their banks, most likely from Mastercard's "Simplified
BIN account range table", which issue #51 points to:
https://www.mastercard.us/en-us/business/issuers/get-support/simplified-bin-account-range-table.html
Added in 2021 (commit 892765a).

Licence: not recorded.


Regexes in pywhat/Data/regex.json
---------------------------------
Five regexes are based on entries of the regex101 community library
(https://regex101.com/library), rewritten for pyWhat in #276. regex101 states no licence for
library entries.
  Browser User Agent            "Parsing browser User Agents"         https://regex101.com/r/aL8lD7/2
  Regex101 Permalink            "regex101.com permalink id grabber"   https://regex101.com/r/wY0rM7/3
  ISO 8601 Timestamp            "RFC3339 DateTime"                    https://regex101.com/r/qH0sU7/1
  United Kingdom (UK) Postcode  "UK Postcode Checker"                 https://regex101.com/r/tH9mQ1/1
  Cron Schedule                 "Cron schedule"                       https://regex101.com/r/vY5eL1/1

Some of the bug bounty regexes are based on the regex database of Dora
(https://github.com/sdushantha/dora):
  Copyright (c) 2021 Siddharth Dushantha, under the MIT License.

Some regexes are based on the patterns of gf (https://github.com/tomnomnom/gf):
